  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+1)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+x+3 & =(Ax+1)x+3({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+1+3 & =(A(1)+1)(1)+3({1}^{2}+1) \\\\ 9 & =(A+1)+3(2) \\\\ 9 & =A+1+6 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
